glsl: bind atan2f to the baseline glibc symbol version

Packaging fix, not a behaviour change: without it the libgallium built on a
host with glibc 2.43 headers cannot be loaded at all by the ChromeOS R149
image, whose glibc is 2.38.

glibc 2.43 added a correctly-rounded atan2f under a new symbol version.
src/compiler/glsl/ir_constant_expression.cpp is the only translation unit in
the whole tree that references atan2f, so that one symbol was single-handedly
raising libgallium's requirement:

  before   readelf --dyn-syms | grep -o 'GLIBC_[0-9.]*' | sort -uV | tail -1
           -> GLIBC_2.43
  after    -> GLIBC_2.38   (matches libvulkan_intel.so and the R149 image)

The two atan2f implementations differ only in last-place rounding, and the
call site is GLSL compile-time constant folding of atan(y, x).

Historically this was done by hand as a post-link binary edit, which is what
made packages/mesa-lnl.tar.gz's libgallium_dri.so non-reproducible from the
build tree (see mesa-patches/README.md). This replaces it.

--- a/src/compiler/glsl/ir_constant_expression.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/glsl/ir_constant_expression.cpp
@@ -34,6 +34,24 @@
  */
 
 #include <math.h>
+
+/* brunch: keep the glibc symbol version floor at the x86-64 baseline.
+ *
+ * glibc 2.43 added a correctly-rounded atan2f under a new symbol version, so a
+ * host toolchain with 2.43 headers emits a reference to atan2f@GLIBC_2.43 --
+ * and this is the only translation unit in the whole tree that references
+ * atan2f, so that single symbol is what pins libgallium's requirement above
+ * the glibc of the ChromeOS R149 image we install into (2.38), where it then
+ * fails to load outright.
+ *
+ * Bind the reference to the baseline version instead. The two implementations
+ * differ only in last-place rounding, and this call site is GLSL compile-time
+ * constant folding of atan(y, x).
+ */
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && defined(__x86_64__)
+__asm__(".symver atan2f,atan2f@GLIBC_2.2.5");
+#endif
+
 #include "util/rounding.h" /* for _mesa_roundeven */
 #include "util/half_float.h"
 #include "ir.h"
